// An instance has a reference only while it exists, as it has children only while it exists
// (gsdlab/clafer#122, reading A of kbak/clafer-semantics#168). So an obligation on the value of
// an instance holds only if the instance exists: x must exist in the second state to have the
// value 7 there. A value that x would have after it disappears is not a value.

x -> integer ?
    [ initially X (this.dref = 7) ]
[ initially some x ]

assert [ initially X some x ]
